questions.question:
After the fix, a learner who submits too fast gets:

HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests
Content-Type: application/problem+json
Retry-After: 30
{"type":"https://api.codedev.test/problems/rate-limited","status":429,"code":"rate_limited","detail":"Retry in 30 seconds."}

The web client's submit loop:

for (let attempt = 0; attempt < 5; attempt++) {
  const res = await submit(payload);
  if (res.status !== 429) return res;
  await sleep(1000 * 2 ** attempt);   // 1, 2, 4, 8, 16 s
}
throw new Error("Too many requests");

Statement: "This loop handles the 429 well: exponential backoff spaces the retries out, so it does not need to read Retry-After."
